# If else inside a range loop executes both branches

Verifies the range-loop execution planner preserves an else branch instead of
using the comparison-only fast path that represents only the true branch.

>>> source
for (index in 0..3) {
    if (index == 1) {
        print("match")
    } else {
        print("other")
    }
}

<<< stdout
other
match
other

<<< stderr
